---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
	title="Terms of Use"
	description="The terms governing your use of DayAlmanac."
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px]">
		<h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--ink)] md:text-4xl">Terms of Use</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-[var(--ink)]/40">Last updated: July 31, 2026</p>

		<div class="prose-content mt-7 max-w-[640px] text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.85] text-[var(--ink)]/70">
			<p>
				These Terms of Use govern your access to and use of {SITE_TITLE} (dayalmanac.com, the
				"Site"). By using the Site, you agree to these terms.
			</p>

			<h2>Content</h2>
			<p>
				DayAlmanac publishes reference content about observances, public holidays, awareness
				periods and other calendar dates: when each falls, what it is, and who established it.
				Articles reflect our own research at the time of publication and are provided for general
				informational purposes only, not as professional, legal, or academic advice.
			</p>

			<h2>Dates</h2>
			<p>
				Date tables on this Site are generated from the stated rule and checked against published
				authorities, and each page cites the source of its rule. They are still a secondary
				source. Rules can be amended, observances can be moved or discontinued, and the same
				observance is sometimes kept on different dates in different countries or organisations.
				Before committing to anything that matters — booking travel, scheduling paid time off,
				setting a campaign or filing date — confirm the date against the official body that owns
				it. We are not liable for losses arising from reliance on a date published here.
			</p>

			<h2>Intellectual property</h2>
			<p>
				Unless otherwise noted, the text and original graphics on this Site are owned by DayAlmanac.
				You're welcome to link to our articles or quote brief excerpts with attribution. Republishing
				full articles elsewhere without permission isn't allowed.
			</p>

			<h2>Third-party links and ads</h2>
			<p>
				The Site may display ads served by advertising partners and may link to third-party sites.
				We aren't responsible for the content, accuracy, or practices of external sites we link to or
				that serve ads on this Site. See our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for how advertising
				cookies work.
			</p>

			<h2>No warranty</h2>
			<p>
				The Site is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. We try to keep articles
				accurate and up to date but make no guarantee that content is complete, current, or free of
				errors.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				We may update these terms as the Site evolves. Continued use of the Site after changes take
				effect means you accept the updated terms.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about these terms can be sent to Owen Zhang via the contact information on the
				<a href="/about/">About</a> page.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.prose-content :global(h2) {
		margin-top: 1.75rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
		color: var(--ink);
	}
	.prose-content :global(h2:first-child) {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.prose-content :global(p) {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.prose-content :global(a) {
		color: var(--flag-dark);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
</style>
